        <p class="lede">
          Short answer: Dymatize ISO100 is the best hydrolyzed whey protein for most buyers, because it pairs hydrolyzed whey isolate with ordinary isolate at a mid-range price and tastes like a normal shake. Optimum Nutrition Platinum Hydrowhey is the pick if you want hydrolysate as the main protein and a 30 g serving, and Rule 1 R1 Protein is the value option built only on isolate and hydrolysate. Be clear on what you are paying for, though. In the research we cover below, hydrolyzed whey digests a little faster, but over weeks of training it has not built more muscle than a well-made isolate. It earns its premium for a narrow group of people, mostly those whose stomachs still complain after switching to isolate.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

